      "html": "<ul><li>A schedule of condition records a property at lease start. A dilapidations schedule lists the repairs owed at lease end.</li><li>The schedule of condition is often attached to the lease. How far it limits the tenant's repairs depends on how the lease words it.</li><li>Section 18(1) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1927 caps damages for breach of a repairing covenant at the amount by which the breach reduces the value of the landlord's reversion.</li><li>Photos taken on site decide a dispute. Do not rebuild them at your desk.</li><li>You pay £75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts.</li><li>The app helps you record. It does not give legal advice.</li></ul>"
